{
 "section_summary": "This section moves from the end of an industrial disarmament paper to an occupation report on Japanese production, legal reform, and press reactions to the surrender anniversary. Memoranda then debate how to balance reparations claimants’ preferences against Japan’s need to retain industrial capacity. The remainder contains a covering despatch and SCAP directives selecting chemical, steel, power, machine tool, munitions, and shipbuilding facilities for custody and possible removal, with plant lists and implementation guidance.",
